      "mergedPostDetails": "I saw the announcement for the Creator Toolkit Update Beta, and tried it out. When setting everything up for the Creator Companion, including the prerequisites necessary to run the program, I tried to migrate an existing project I was working on only a day before the update.\nI selected the project file, and clicked \"Migrate\", then \"Migrate to copy.\" It began copying files over into the \"[project name]-Directory\" folder, but paused prematurely when trying to copy a specific file. After letting it sit for two hours, there was no change in anything. The \"Migrating...\" window was still stuck on the main page, but the program was still running, it just wasn't copying or sending any info.\nThe companion is still technically usable, as you can click on anything within the companion, including the logs, and the tools, but the page is still active, and only disappears after you restart the program.\nI've already tried to restart the process twice, with the same result. It still works with creating a new project, and importing a different file, but it just freezes on this particular project.",
      "mergedPostTitle": "[softlock BETA] Client softlocks and freezes when migrating a copy of an existing project.",
